  "query_preview": "..\nA very dry pattern is now entrenched across the Marianas, with only\nspotty light showers evident on the latest radar data. Typhoon In-fa\nis seen to the east-northeast of Saipan, moving steadily toward the\nnorthern CNMI. However, convection and the wind field remain close to\nthe center. Therefore, not expecting to see much activity south of\nAlamagan. Over the next week, POPs will range from 0 to 20 percent\nacross the Marianas. For Sunday and Monday, light and variable winds\nwill allow island convection to develop over Guam and possibly the\nCNMI. By Tuesday, winds look to be a bit stronger, decreasing the\nlikelihood of island effect showers.",
